 "text": "What if everyone on earth woke up 10% Nigerian? Not a little bit. Exactly 10%. And your family found out first. Day 1. An auntie you've never met calls you at 6am. She knows your full name, your salary, and that you're still single. She hangs up before you can ask who she is. Day 3. Your mom calls you this boy in the middle of the supermarket. 9 times. Now strangers are calling you this boy too. Week 1. The office party has two pots of geloff. By 3pm it's a full argument about who's is better. It ends with HR, a written warning, and nobody returning the plates. Week 3. Every house on your street buys a generator. Just in case. Nobody's power has gone off, they argue about who's is louder anyway. Month 2. Weddings now last three days. You have four this weekend. You've spent 2,400 euros on matching outfits, and you've only met one of the couples. Month 6. The visa queue at the embassy stretches 41 kilometers. People bring folding chairs and coolers of food. At the front, the answer is still no. Year 1. We have food at home becomes the most said sentence on earth. Fast food sales drop 31%. Burger chains quietly add joe loft to the menu. Year 5. Every stadium plays afro beats at halftime. Even funerals have a DJ now. Nobody remembers what a quiet afternoon sounds like. Year 10. You finally become a doctor. Your mom hugs you, cries, and asks when you're getting married. What should happen next?"
